[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1734","stub":{"id":"1734","section":"Highway 68 to Hiwassee River","altname":"","river":"Coker Creek","difficulty":"IIItoIVstandoutV","states":["USA-TNN"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"1.12","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"levelFT","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112364","location":{"latitude":"35.218102","longitude":"-84.3414"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"this is a straight forward 4 foot ledege drop, best run boofing right, to set up for the next drop.","id":"912","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"First Drop","distance":"0.1","difficulty":"III+","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"waterfall","description":"Run driving right to left, waiting for the bounce half way down. Let it keep you flat and angled left.","id":"913","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Coker Creek Falls","distance":"0.1","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":"380"},{"type":"waterfall","description":"Some troughy entrance ledges that can be very shallow precede this 12 foot drop that can be run right or left. On the left there will be some bounce!","id":"914","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Hiding Place Falls","distance":"0.2","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":"6274"},{"type":"waterfall","description":"At the top is a kinder smaller less undercut notch from the Green, fanning out onto a domed ledge dropping 10 feet. I like to boof with slight right angle, and finish right. There are a number of lines, but there is a pin bottom left to be aware of","id":"910","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Turkey Tail","distance":"0.3","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":"6482"},{"type":"hazard","description":"This drop lands from nine feet onto rocks. There is a line on the left that is currently unpleasant due to the mountain laurel and ill place pin rocks, but you wont have to get out of your boat","id":"909","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Hidden Abashment","distance":"0.4","photoID":null,"difficulty":"III+","approximate":false},{"type":"hazard","description":"This is out of context. It's long and complicated, so take a look your first time. At levels of 4-8 inches, seriously consider walking, no matter how fun it looks. The undercut is sicko.","id":"908","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Snakedance","distance":"0.5","photoID":null,"difficulty":"V","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117648","location":{"latitude":"35.179298","longitude":"-84.395302"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"6","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"100261871","title":null,"post_date":"2008-03-03 05:00:00+00","detail":"Josh and Tyler...\nWe attempted to run the creek on 03/01/08 extremely low level...we scraped over Coker falls and decided to just scout the rest of the big stuff, finding ample new trees in the run...It looks like hidden abashment has 2 new logs making it a portage and the intro to snake dance has a good sized pine blocking it as well. If we would have had a good bow saw and a few more hands, most of the trees could have been removed with in a reasonable time...as far as the rest of the run, we ran out of day light to continue. most of the other logs we saw wouldn't effect the upper section too much...Just keep your eyes open....it's an awesome place and well worth the trip.","user":null}],"photos":[{"id":"6482","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5467","description":"You can see the big pourover. Boof right or straight down the middle with speed.","caption":"Turkey Tail","poi_name":"Bubble Notch","subject":"","author":"Kirk Eddlemon","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.ameri